Key numbers: F_FULLFSYNC costs about 4.1 ms per file, which would add roughly 2 minutes to 30k files, while fsync(2) costs about 45 µs per file. Per-byte cost is small (about 1 s per GiB for write plus hash). That leaves the 13 s copy time unexplained, so I'll break the copy into read, write, and chmod passes before deriving a budget from it.
