 **Decisions needing a yes or no from you.**
-- **D1. Hard-link cost.** Unchanged files are hard-linked, costing about 0.39 ms each per run, so about 12 s per 30 000 files every run. The alternative is a content-addressed store (`objects/<sha256>` plus a per-snapshot index). Per-run filesystem work would then be O(changed files), with O(F) index bytes (about 0.1 s for 30 000 entries). But it breaks the directory-snapshot assumption behind the `snaputil` helpers, needs mark-and-sweep under `.lock` for deletion, and changes the restore contract. This design chooses hard links. Confirm, or choose the store.
